QUESTION_PROMPT_BEGIN bytes=370
Find KE of product particles in,
Pi(+) = mu(+) + nu
here Pi(+) is stationary.
Rest mass of Pi(+) & mu(+) is 139.6 MeV & 105.7 MeV respectively.

Choices:
A. 7.2 MeV, 32.8 MeV
B. 4.12 MeV, 29.8 MeV
C. 2.84 MeV, 26.8 MeV
D. 3.52 MeV, 20.8 MeV

Solve the question. At the end, write exactly one final line in this format and do not write anything after it:
Answer: <letter>
QUESTION_PROMPT_END
MODEL_OUTPUT_BEGIN bytes=1102
We have the decay:  
π⁺ → μ⁺ + ν  
π⁺ at rest, so initial momentum = 0.  
Masses:  
m_π = 139.6 MeV/c²  
m_μ = 105.7 MeV/c²  
m_ν ≈ 0  

Energy conservation:  
m_π c² = E_μ + E_ν  
Momentum conservation:  
p_μ = p_ν (magnitudes equal, opposite directions).  

For neutrino: E_ν = p_ν c (since massless).  
For muon: E_μ = √(p_μ² c² + m_μ² c⁴).  

Let p = p_μ c = p_ν c (in energy units).  
Then:  
√(p² + m_μ²) + p = m_π  

Solve:  
√(p² + m_μ²) = m_π - p  
Square:  
p² + m_μ² = m_π² - 2 m_π p + p²  
⇒ m_μ² = m_π² - 2 m_π p  
⇒ 2 m_π p = m_π² - m_μ²  
⇒ p = (m_π² - m_μ²) / (2 m_π)  

Numerically:  
m_π² = (139.6)² = 19488.16  
m_μ² = (105.7)² = 11172.49  
Difference = 8315.67  
Divide by 2 m_π = 279.2 → p = 8315.67 / 279.2 ≈ 29.78 MeV/c  

Then:  
E_ν = p ≈ 29.78 MeV (kinetic energy, since massless).  
E_μ = m_π - p = 139.6 - 29.78 = 109.82 MeV  
Muon KE = E_μ - m_μ = 109.82 - 105.7 = 4.12 MeV  

Thus KE: muon = 4.12 MeV, neutrino = 29.78 MeV ≈ 29.8 MeV.  

That matches choice B.  

Answer: B
MODEL_OUTPUT_END

