We are given:

(1) \( 2Fe(s) + \frac{3}{2}O_2(g) \rightarrow Fe_2O_3(s) \) with \(\Delta G = -177\) kcal  
(2) \( 4Fe_2O_3(s) + Fe(s) \rightarrow 3Fe_3O_4(s) \) with \(\Delta G = -19\) kcal  

We need the Gibbs free energy of formation of \(Fe_3O_4\) (per mole).

Let \(\Delta G_f(Fe_2O_3) = -177\) kcal/mol (since reaction (1) forms 1 mole of Fe₂O₃).  
Let \(\Delta G_f(Fe_3O_4) = x\) kcal/mol (unknown).  
For reaction (2):  
\(\Delta G = 3\Delta G_f(Fe_3O_4) - 4\Delta G_f(Fe_2O_3) - \Delta G_f(Fe)\).  
But \(\Delta G_f(Fe) = 0\) for pure element. So:  
\(-19 = 3x - 4(-177) = 3x + 708\).  
Thus \(3x = -19 - 708 = -727\) → \(x = -727/3 = -242.333...\) kcal/mol.

That matches choice D: \(-242.3\) kcal/mol.

Answer: D
